# A trusted room's shell reads the toolchain (the architect's decision of
# 2026-11-09, ADR-0172): on the tour's image, which has /bin and /usr, a
# terminal launched in a room holds the room's grants and +r /bin, +r /usr
# and +r /etc, and runs POSIX programs from them. Coordinates as in
# tests/gui/rooms.script: the second terminal's frame at (104, 102), the
# room's chip found by room.1 (2f7f8f) on the dock's row, d3e1e5 the
# focused ground tinted by room.1.
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type mkdir project\r
screen ~> _
type room new project +w ~/project\r
screen project --colour 1 +w ~/project
screen ~> _
clickc 2f7f8f 300 719 600 7
chord meta ret
origin 105 138
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen project ~/project> _
click 400 120
region 162 108 100 4 d3e1e5
# A pipeline of the shell's echo and the volume's tr, then ls and uname.
type echo hi | tr h H\r
screen Hi
screen project ~/project> _
type echo a > a.txt; ls\r
screen a.txt
screen project ~/project> _
type uname\r
screen Zoraya
screen project ~/project> _
# The first terminal's shell turns the machine off.
click 400 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
origin 73 106
type poweroff\r
exit
